why: the note opens on an actor the site does not name and uses a name the reader cannot place; Kirill on 2026-09-21: "This looks out of blue and hard to follow"; the fix that day was a rule putting the site's subject first, and the rule of 2026-09-21 reverses it so the fact keeps its own subject, which is what the barred wording is here for: the fact's own subject is the outside thing the fact is about, and a chooser the code never names is not one; the expected form places the outside name with an appositive, and no check reaches this, so judgement decides it; on 2026-09-23 the rules that put a note's fact before its tie took this case from 5 of 15 on main to 0, both under its floor; the fact's subject is the ledger, so every roll opens on it with the barred verb and then ties the fact to the function correctly; recorded failing as the second residual those rules carry, beside k17, and a blind reader built to catch it was measured on 2026-09-23 and deleted by its bar, so code review is where this residual is caught
